  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Tripartite constituents effectively engage in social dialogue to apply labour regulations and international labour standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Timor-Leste actively advances a green economy in line with the Paris Agreement. However, it remains unclear whether employers and workers are adequately consulted in the development of climate policies. Given the significant impact of climate change on businesses, employment, and livelihoods, it is crucial to foster social dialogue and collaboration between employers, workers, and the government. Effective social dialogue is key to advancing frameworks for a transition to greener economies and promoting greater formality within the labour market.
During this biennium, the ILO initiative focuses on developing comprehensive frameworks that support just transitions and improve industrial relations through collaboration among the government, employers, and workers. The ILO continues raising awareness among the National Labour Council, the Ministry of Environment, and other relevant government bodies about the challenges posed by climate change. Efforts also focus on strengthening social dialogue capacities and identifying priorities for a Just Transition. These initiatives aim to establish a framework agreement that promotes sustainable business practices, improves labour relations, and aligns climate actions with job creation and economic growth. The goal is to ensure that climate action fosters both business sustainability and decent work for all.</narrative>
  </description>
